WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.873
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.173 --> 00:00:09.571
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.871 --> 00:00:17.271
Unit ten: Causative and Other Structures: Have, Get and Let. Today you will say that someone else does something for you.

4
00:00:17.571 --> 00:00:20.131
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:24.276
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:26.083
Causative.

7
00:00:27.083 --> 00:00:30.209
Causative means showing that someone causes an action.

8
00:00:30.817 --> 00:00:32.514
Have is causative here.

9
00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:35.862
Your turn. Say: Causative.

10
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.689
Causative.

11
00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:41.439
Repair.

12
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.066
Repair means to fix.

13
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.383
I had my phone repaired.

14
00:00:46.983 --> 00:00:49.810
Your turn. Say: Repair.

15
00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:53.575
Repair.

16
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:55.202
Haircut.

17
00:00:56.217 --> 00:00:58.263
Haircut means a short hair style.

18
00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.014
I had a haircut.

19
00:01:00.617 --> 00:01:02.909
Your turn. Say: Haircut.

20
00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:06.640
Haircut.

21
00:01:07.383 --> 00:01:08.222
Allow.

22
00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:11.135
Allow means to let someone do.

23
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.169
They allow us to enter.

24
00:01:13.783 --> 00:01:15.960
Your turn. Say: Allow.

25
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:19.848
Allow.

26
00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:21.433
Make.

27
00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:23.950
Make means to force.

28
00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.178
The teacher made us stay.

29
00:01:26.783 --> 00:01:29.122
Your turn. Say: Make.

30
00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:32.863
Make.

31
00:01:33.617 --> 00:01:34.316
Let.

32
00:01:35.317 --> 00:01:36.736
Let means to allow.

33
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.374
Let me help you.

34
00:01:38.983 --> 00:01:41.369
Your turn. Say: Let.

35
00:01:44.233 --> 00:01:45.107
Let.

36
00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:46.816
Service.

37
00:01:47.817 --> 00:01:50.014
Service means work done for others.

38
00:01:50.617 --> 00:01:52.140
The service was good.

39
00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.309
Your turn. Say: Service.

40
00:01:58.167 --> 00:01:59.156
Service.

41
00:01:59.917 --> 00:02:00.732
Arrange.

42
00:02:01.717 --> 00:02:03.565
Arrange means to organise.

43
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:05.557
I arranged a meeting.

44
00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.547
Your turn. Say: Arrange.

45
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.459
Arrange.

46
00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:16.790
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.218
Visal, what does have something done mean?

48
00:02:21.317 --> 00:02:31.274
It means someone else does the job for you. I had my phone repaired means a technician fixed it. The pattern is have plus object plus past participle.

49
00:02:32.383 --> 00:02:33.593
Is get the same?

50
00:02:34.683 --> 00:02:43.570
Yes, get something done is more informal: She got her hair cut. Get can also show a problem, such as He got his bag stolen.

51
00:02:44.683 --> 00:02:46.218
What about make and let?

52
00:02:47.317 --> 00:02:59.907
Make and let are followed by the base verb without to: The teacher made us rewrite it, and She let me use her pen. In the passive, make takes to: We were made to rewrite it.

53
00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:03.101
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:08.097
Grammar focus: have plus object plus past participle.

55
00:03:08.397 --> 00:03:09.642
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:12.059
I had my phone repaired.

57
00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:14.555
The teacher made us rewrite it.

58
00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:22.506
Use have or get plus an object and a past participle for jobs done by others. Make and let take the base verb without to.

59
00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:27.087
Be careful! Don't say: I had repaired my phone.

60
00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:31.300
Say: I had my phone repaired.

61
00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.925
have + object + V3.

62
00:03:34.733 --> 00:03:37.223
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.371
At the Repair Shop.

64
00:03:39.671 --> 00:03:42.158
Mealea had her phone repaired last week.

65
00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:45.422
She also got her hair cut on Saturday.

66
00:03:46.433 --> 00:03:48.897
The technician let her watch the repair.

67
00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:51.830
He made her sign a form first.

68
00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:55.355
Next month she will have her bike serviced.

69
00:03:56.467 --> 00:04:00.643
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:01.483 --> 00:04:03.529
Have + object + blank.

71
00:04:03.829 --> 00:04:07.901
A, -ing. B, past participle. C, base verb.

72
00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:14.232
The answer is B: past participle.

73
00:04:15.383 --> 00:04:16.930
The teacher made us blank.

74
00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:20.802
A, to rewrite. B, rewriting. C, rewrite.

75
00:04:24.367 --> 00:04:26.506
The answer is C: rewrite.

76
00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.348
She let me blank her pen.

77
00:04:29.648 --> 00:04:33.081
A, use. B, to use. C, using.

78
00:04:36.633 --> 00:04:38.598
The answer is A: use.

79
00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.622
Got her hair cut means blank.

80
00:04:41.922 --> 00:04:45.622
A, it fell. B, someone cut it. C, she cut it.

81
00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:51.259
The answer is B: someone cut it.

82
00:04:52.417 --> 00:04:54.114
What did Mealea have repaired?

83
00:04:54.414 --> 00:04:57.836
A, her bike. B, her bag. C, her phone.

84
00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.400
The answer is C: her phone.

85
00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.891
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.390
What have you had done recently?

87
00:05:19.183 --> 00:05:20.649
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:20.949 --> 00:05:28.921
I had my hair cut last week. I also had my bicycle repaired. Next month I will have my school uniform made.

89
00:05:29.221 --> 00:05:31.325
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:32.217 --> 00:05:37.493
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and have plus object plus past participle.

91
00:05:37.793 --> 00:05:43.139
Today's value is practical wisdom. Judge ideas by how well they work in real life.

92
00:05:43.439 --> 00:05:46.033
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

93
00:05:46.333 --> 00:05:50.541
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

